In `adjust_message_entities_to_utf_16`, the loop runs over `enumerate(positions)`, so its iteration count is exactly `len(positions)`. The code builds `positions` by taking, for each entity, the pair `(x.offset, x.offset + x.length)`, flattening all those pairs, and sorting them. The test passes 9 entities, so that produces `2 * 9 = 18` position values. Sorting does not change the count, so the loop executes 18 iterations.

